            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run: what did atithi mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: నిజం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నిజం (nijaṁ) — \"true; the truth\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit nija meant \"one's own, innate\" — what belongs to a thing by its nature. Telugu moved it one step: what belongs to a thing by nature is what is really so, and నిజం (nijaṁ) became the truth."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Alone it answers a doubt: nijaṁ, \"true\". With a question on the end it becomes perhaps the commonest interjection in the language: nijamā?, \"really?\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five answers that are neither అవును nor లేదు."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "nijaṁ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *nijaṁ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "nijaṁ, then nijamā?, and say which one asks",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *nijaṁ*, then *nijamā?*, and say which one asks]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does నిజం (nijaṁ) mean? (\"true; the truth\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
