        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: చాలు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చాలు (cālu) — \"enough, that will do\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చాలు (cālu) is a verb — \"it suffices\" — used as a complete answer. Held over a glass being filled it stops the pouring; said of an argument it ends it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చాలా, the everyday word for \"very\" and \"a lot\", is the same root wearing a different ending. Sufficiency and abundance sit one letter apart, which is a fair account of how the two ideas are related anywhere."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
