          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తప్పకుండా (tappakuṇḍā) — \"certainly, without fail\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Take it apart: తప్పు, \"to miss, to slip, to go wrong\", plus -కుండా, the ending meaning \"without doing\". తప్పకుండా (tappakuṇḍā) is without missing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The ending is worth having on its own, because it attaches to any verb stem: ceppakuṇḍā, without telling; tinakuṇḍā, without eating. One suffix, and every verb you own gains a negative."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
