            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did ēmō mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: అలాగే",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అలాగే (alāgē) — \"just so, alright then\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అలా means \"in that way\"; -గే is the small emphatic tail that makes it \"just so\". అలాగే (alāgē) is the yes you give to an instruction — not \"that is correct\" but \"it shall be as you said\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Now look at the front of it. అ- points far, and already carries అది, \"that one\", and అక్కడ, \"there\". ఇ- points near: ఇది, ఇక్కడ, and so ఇలా, \"in this way\". ఎ- asks: ఎక్కడ, ఎలా. Three vowels, one grid, and అలాగే (alāgē) is simply the far corner of it with an ending stuck on."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five answers, and a three-way grid you can now see running under అది, ఇక్కడ and ఎలా."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
